  "dossier": "Wrote 2 letters from Naples (1640) petitioning the General for the foreign missions; requested destination: East Indies (2).",
  "letters": [
   {
    "n": 111,
    "year": 1640,
    "date": "February 24, 1640",
    "place": "Naples",
    "archival": "ARSI, FG 742, 248",
    "excerpt": "With a lively hope and an inward sentiment I feel moved today, which is the feast of Saint Matthias, to write to Your Paternity on a matter of election, since no good fortune can be hoped for but where Saint Matthias enters as advocate, to whom so happy a lot once fell. Your Paternity knows the desire which God of His grace has granted me, to go and serve Him as His laborer in the Indies; and I do not doubt in the least that the Lord has destined me to be a missioner in those parts, since He never ceases to call me and invite me continually.",
    "kind": "abridged",
    "full_paras": [
     "With a lively hope and an inward sentiment I feel moved today, which is the feast of Saint Matthias, to write to Your Paternity on a matter of election, since no good fortune can be hoped for but where Saint Matthias enters as advocate, to whom so happy a lot once fell. Your Paternity knows the desire which God of His grace has granted me, to go and serve Him as His laborer in the Indies; and I do not doubt in the least that the Lord has destined me to be a missioner in those parts, since He never ceases to call me and invite me continually. Now I have spoken here with the Father Procurator of Portugal, whom I understand must be provided with a companion as far as Portugal. I have offered myself to him, even as a servant; and His Reverence does not refuse me, but with sincere affection refers everything to the election of Your Paternity, to whom he tells me he will write, and whom the Father Assistant of Portugal will also beseech in my favor. So I can now say to Your Paternity, whom I hold in the place of God: In manibus tuis sortes meae, Ostende quem elegeris. Ecce me, Pater, ad omnia paratum (in thy hands are my lots; show whom thou hast chosen. Behold me, Father, ready for all things). If Your Paternity has so often consoled and enkindled me with good hopes, let good fortune now console me upon myself. I, prostrate with all affection before the feet of Your Paternity, beg in Visceribus Christi (in the heart of Christ) to grant me this grace: to give me as companion to the Father Procurator of Portugal, from whence I may then depart for the Indies at the first embarkation. I hope in my Lord Jesus Christ that He will inspire this thought in Your Paternity, while I remain meanwhile with all humility awaiting from His hands my blessed lot. And I commend myself most humbly to His holy Sacrifices."
    ]
   },
   {
    "n": 129,
    "year": 1640,
    "date": "December 29, 1640",
    "place": "Naples",
    "archival": "ARSI, FG 742, 424",
    "excerpt": "The scruple of not wishing to be indiscreet by multiplying letters to Your Paternity more often on the same matter has sufficed to restrain me for some three months from writing to you, and from renewing the memory of the holy desires which God of His grace